<title>FRANCE: French planters see '96 sugar output at 4.2 mln T.</title>
<headline>French planters see '96 sugar output at 4.2 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>French sugar beet planters confirmed on Thursday they saw 1996/97 sugar output at 4.2 million tonnes, unchanged from the previous season.</p>
<p>&quot;The crop is better than initially expected. Sugar content is excellent. We should reach a sugar output of 4.2 million tonnes,&quot; the president of the CGB planters federation Dominique Ducroquet told a news conference.</p>
<p>Ducroquet linked the performance to exceptional sugar content, which could reach a record 19 percent.</p>
<p>Final beet yields may reach 66-67 tonnes per hectare, unchanged from last year. --Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
